    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "us ); wealth alone be ours, without which all these virtues",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "are like ( of as little worth as ) a piece of straw.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "40. There are the limbs, all the same; the action the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "same; the same unimpaired intellect; and speech also the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "same; and yet the same man, destitute of the warmth of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "wealth, becomes instantaneously a changed being; this is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "strange.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "41. The man who possesses wealth is ( considered ) noble-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "born; he is learned, well-informed, and an appreciator of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "merits; he alone is an orator and a handsome man; (in short)",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "all qualifications cling to wealth.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "42. On account of evil counsel is ruined a king; an an-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "chorite by attachment to worldly pleasures; a son by indul-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "gence; a Bráhmaṇa by not studying the Vedas; a family by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "a misbehaved son; character by association with the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "wicked; modesty by wine; husbandry by want of attention;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "affection by resorting to travel; friendship by want of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "courtesy; prosperity by bad management; and wealth by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "misdirected charity ( or careless expenditure).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "43. Charity, enjoyment, and destruction are the three",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "courses by which wealth passes away. He who neither gives",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "nor enjoys has the third course ( left for his wealth ).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "44. A jewel polished on the grindstone, a victorious",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "warrior wounded with weapons, an elephant emaciated on",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "account of rutting, a river with its waters ( lit. sandy bed )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "shrunken in winter, the moon with an only digit remaining,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "a young woman become languid though amorous sports, and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "persons whose wealth has been bestowed on supplicants—",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "all these look graceful by their slenderness.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r8": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "45. When poor, a man longs for a handful of rice; when",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "afterwards he is full ( of wealth ) he regards the whole earth",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
